15:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-10 text-lg leading-8","children":["$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"font-medium text-ink","children":"TSA officers at Miami International Airport find live baby snakes and tortoises hidden in a traveler's underwear."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-6 text-ink-soft","children":"Simon Turola Borges, a 30-year-old Brazilian national, was pulled aside by TSA officers at Miami International Airport on August 25, 2011, after a body scanner flagged him ahead of a flight home. Officers found two hatchling pythons wrapped in pantyhose in his cargo pants pockets, and when he pulled back the waistband of his underwear, more nylon-wrapped snakes and tortoises fell out. In total, agents recovered three ball pythons, three carpet pythons, one children's python, one Indian star tortoise, and two leopard tortoises, all several-week-old hatchlings protected under international wildlife trade law. Borges pleaded guilty to smuggling and was sentenced to time served, two years of supervised release, and a $400 fine paid to the Miami Science Museum."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-10 rounded-xl bg-paper-soft p-6","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-ink","children":"Score breakdown"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-4","children":[["$","div","Absurdity",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-1.5 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 text-sm font-medium","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Absurdity"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"#FF6B35"},"children":[22,"/",25]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"h-2.5 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-line","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"h-full rounded-full","style":{"width":"88%","backgroundColor":"#FF6B35"}}]}]]}],["$","div","Humor",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-1.5 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 text-sm font-medium","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Humor"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":